#
# Conformance case: teleology/conditional-false-guard (issue #1055 W1, Task 5).
#
# A conditional goal whose guard situation is FALSE at the last state → the goal prescribes nothing (Satisfaction::DoesNotApply, no satisfactionStatus quad) + Completed (does-not-apply, NOT Unsatisfied).
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/conditional-false-guard/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
